# Read by ESP-IDF as a component Kconfig, and by both forges' `make menu`
# (scripts/menu.py) for the UWB_<CHIP> prompts. stm-forge has no Kconfig
# build step: its build only sees the defconfig lines, as
# -DCONFIG_UWB_<CHIP>=1 or 0. Every chip is off unless set.
# Outside ESP-IDF, CMakeLists.txt takes its options from the bool entries
# here, found by their type line: keep `bool` directly under each `config`.
menuconfig UWB
    bool "UWB transceiver subsystem"
    default y
    help
        The UWB core: struct uwb_dev, uwb_send(), uwb_recv(), the hardware
        timestamps and the uwb_* log helpers. Pick the chip drivers you need
        below; none is built by default, so a chip missing from sdkconfig is
        off.

if UWB

    config UWB_DW1000
        bool "Decawave DW1000 (SPI, two-way ranging)"
        default n
        help
            Build the DW1000 driver: dw1000_init(), dw1000_twr_range() and
            friends.

    config UWB_DEBUG
        bool "uwb_dbg() lines"
        default n
        help
            STM32 HAL only: compile uwb_dbg() lines in. On ESP-IDF uwb_dbg()
            is ESP_LOGD and the log level decides.

endif # UWB
